      "writtenOn": "2021-10-26T16:49:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. OK, I will move this to CLs where it is used\n\n2. PS8xxx emulator has its own DTS node with phandle to TCPCI emulator. PS8xxx register itself as an extension using tcpci_emul_set_dev_ops(). I2C messages goes to TCPCI emulator which call dev_ops. In dev_ops callback, PS8xxx handles its specific registers (e.g. FW_REV) or gives control back to generic TCPCI.\n\nI am considering to add function ps8xxx_emul_get_tcpci() to get pointer to TCPCI emulator which can be used with tcpci_emul_* functions.\n\n3. TCPCI emulator uses i2c_emul_register() for main address. PS8xxx emulator uses i2c_emul_register() only for secondary addresses (p0, p1 and gpio).\n\nI would expect that other TCPCI devices don\u0027t have secondary addresses, then only TCPCI emulator will use i2c_emul_register() and device emulator will use only tcpci_emul_set_dev_ops()",
      "parentUuid": "20d90822_217bf747",
      "revId": "58761e9e3db671f612ab14c12e50e16c0545993b",
